    <h1 style="font-size:2rem;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Julian Perez</h1>
    <p style="color:#555;margin-bottom:2rem;">DJ · Producer · Record Label Founder · Ibiza Underground Resident</p>

    <h2>Biography</h2>
    <p>Julian Perez developed his connection to electronic music in the early 1990s, shaped by the House and Techno scenes emerging from the US, the UK, and Northwestern Europe. Genres such as Techno, EBM, and New Beat played a key role in defining his sound, which has evolved with patience, discernment, and a deep respect for the culture. Over time, he became known as a versatile DJ whose approach favors long-term vision over immediacy.</p>

    <p>In 2010, he released his first record, marking the beginning of a steadily built career. Two years later, he founded Fathers & Sons Productions (2012), a vinyl-only label created as a platform to share his distinctive sound. Within its first year, the label hosted showcases in more than twelve countries and established a solid catalog of releases.</p>

    <p>Alongside his own imprints, Julian's music has appeared on respected labels such as Cocoon Recordings, Raum..Musik, and Subwax Bcn, further cementing his reputation as both producer and tastemaker.</p>

    <p>To date, every release on his labels has sold out within days, underlining his curatorial instincts and his ability to identify emerging talent.</p>

    <h2>Discography Highlights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Solemnity</strong> (2016) — Debut solo album, double vinyl. Released on Fathers & Sons Productions. Marked a defining chapter of the label.</li>
      <li><strong>Break-Even</strong> (2021) — Second studio album. Released on Girada Unlimited as the label's tenth release.</li>
      <li>Releases on <strong>Cocoon Recordings</strong>, <strong>Raum..Musik</strong>, <strong>Subwax Bcn</strong> and own labels since 2010.</li>
      <li>Every release on his labels has sold out within days of publication.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Record Labels</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Fathers & Sons Productions</strong> (founded 2012, Spain) — Vinyl-only electronic music record label. Within its first year hosted showcases in more than twelve countries. Released Julian's debut album Solemnity (2016). Relaunched in 2023 with renewed focus and forward-looking vision.</li>
      <li><strong>Girada Unlimited</strong> (founded 2017) — Electronic music label that gained strong underground support before Julian's involvement was widely known. Its tenth release was Julian's second album Break-Even (2021). Continues to evolve with releases by Julian and a curated roster of artists.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Live Career</h2>
    <p>Throughout his career, Julian has performed in more than <strong>50 countries and over 150 cities</strong>.</p>

